  "slug": "application-glycomics-massmatchr-01d4",
  "summary": "Recent bioinformatics tools automate glycan annotation of MALDI-TOF peaks and validate glycopeptide identifications across multiple search engines.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is software for interpreting glycan mass spectrometry data, covering post-identification review and peak-level annotation. GlycoViz is presented as an open-source glycoproteomics tool that adds a glycopeptide validation algorithm to post-identification review, with compatibility across multiple search engines and visualization of results. massMatchR, an open-source R/Shiny application, maps MALDI-TOF m/z peaks to a user-defined glycan database to provide automated annotation and structured export. A correction notice for massMatchR, which provides no abstract, is also indexed in this set. What is new is post-identification validation compatible with multiple search engines, and automated, database-driven annotation of glycomics MALDI-TOF peaks within an interactive R/Shiny interface.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-10-03"
}
